{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486382-simple-question-why-twist-are-not-present-in-the-rest-of-the-cofd-line","id":1486382,"title":"Simple question: Why Twist are not present in the rest of the CofD line?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-13T20:44:10-07:00","id":1486382,"title":"Simple question: Why Twist are not present in the rest of the CofD line?","content":"This is something I was thinking comparing books for a little homebrew, and Twist [alternative rules] from Vampire Requiem 2e are not present [or at least, not at the same level] in any other work of CofD I read until now.<br /> <br /> Is there a reason for alternative rules being so present on Vampire Requiem 2e but not on Mage or Werewolf? I even can't think on &quot;what alternative rules I would like to see&quot;, I only can say the alternative rules on Vampire are things I can't imagine neither before read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T02:35:39-07:00","id":1486398,"title":"","content":"Because Requiem Second Edition has managed to get more supplements.<br /> <br /> Mage is still waiting on its book about the Pentacle Orders, anything dedicated to alternate rules is way off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T04:10:39-07:00","id":1486400,"title":"","content":"They're present in Werewolf from p.284, but it's presented in a different format, so I'd guess it's just a matter of different authors having different priorities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486382-simple-question-why-twist-are-not-present-in-the-rest-of-the-cofd-line?p=1486398#post1486398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Requiem Second Edition has managed to get more supplements.<br /> <br /> Mage is still waiting on its book about the Pentacle Orders, anything dedicated to alternate rules is way off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twists were in the core book of Requiem.<br /> <br /> Plus, Mage isn't totally without alternate rules. The core takes time out to detail a chronicle-building tool that really needs you to be pretty into modern pop music.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T06:20:56-07:00","id":1486406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486382-simple-question-why-twist-are-not-present-in-the-rest-of-the-cofd-line?p=1486400#post1486400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Twists were in the core book of Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, as far as Mage goes I think it refers back to the usual answer for why something is not in that corebook: setting terminology, magic rules, and sample spells are already leaving that thing's word count bursting at the seams. There is literally no room in it for anything that is even slightly extraneous. There are more pressing things to the default Mage gameplay and setting that didn't even get to make the cut so that something like Legacies could be in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T16:53:55-07:00","id":1486476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486382-simple-question-why-twist-are-not-present-in-the-rest-of-the-cofd-line?p=1486406#post1486406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, as far as Mage goes I think it refers back to the usual answer for why something is not in that corebook: setting terminology, magic rules, and sample spells are already leaving that thing's word count bursting at the seams. There is literally no room in it for anything that is even slightly extraneous. There are more pressing things to the default Mage gameplay and setting that didn't even get to make the cut so that something like Legacies could be in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, it bears emphasis again and again: Vampire is one of the mechanically and metaphysically simplest of the monster lines to deal with, not needing to devote pagespace to a recurring otherworld or to everyday antagonists that aren't covered by the same mechanics used for player characters and bluebook mortals. It has the flex room to put optional rules and systems in the space that Werewolf has to dedicate to talking about the Shadow or Promethean needs to use for talking about Firestorms and qashmallim or Mummy requires to talk about cults.<br /> <br /> Tradition and brand recognition are far from the only reasons Requiem has come first in the line order \u2014 it's also the game with arguably the least core material to worry about, which means it can spend wordcount on talking about how to use that core material in unusual ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}